00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.360
(eerie music)

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.500
Shortly before Laurie's ambulance
arrives at the hospital,

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.730
we see a mother taking
her swashbuckling son

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:30.960
into the emergency room.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.650
He's bleeding profusely from the mouth

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.630
and when he drops his towel, we see why.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:37.050
A huge razor blade is
jammed into his gums.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.630
This calls back to an urban legend

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:40.190
about tempered Halloween candy.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:41.240
I remember when I was a kid,

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:42.620
my parents would always have to inspect

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:43.520
my trick-or-treating haul

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.560
to look out for any wrappers
that might've been altered

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.880
in fear of a malicious
neighbor possibly poisoning

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.910
or putting foreign objects into the candy.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.240
That's the implication here.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.030
Michael Myers is not the
only evil in Haddonfield.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.560
Longtime Halloween fans know

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.060
that Michael wasn't intended
to be a recurring character.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.390
John Carpenter and Debra Hill

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:01.040
planned to make it an anthology series

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.450
about various scary stories,

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.240
all taking place on Halloween night.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.410
That's why Halloween III
has almost no relation

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:07.570
to the first two movies.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.770
This pirate costume kid

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:10.770
almost seems to foreshadow Halloween III,

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.570
which, spoiler alert, features
an evil company's plots

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:14.900
to harm trick-or-treaters.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.160
With so much of this movie

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.820
trying to match what happened in the past,

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.500
this one character looks
towards Halloween's future.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.480
Soon after, we're introduced to Karen,

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.380
who was on her way out
of a Halloween party.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:25.540
In true Karen fashion,

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.780
she has a little bit of a public freakout.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:28.832
Roll it.

00:08:28.832 --> 00:08:30.807
(digital whooshing)

00:08:30.807 --> 00:08:32.700
- I'm never going to
another Halloween party

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.470
as long as I live, especially
not at Stevie Mathis' house.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.540
- This is our first crew
reference Easter egg

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.530
because Steve Mathis is the electrician

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:40.720
on this movie's credits.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.670
The only other one that I
can say definitely exists

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.600
is in the staff locker
room at the hospital,

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.520
where one of the lockers
is labeled Cummings,

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:47.640
which has got to be a self nod

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.720
by a set decorator, Peg Cummings.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.250
- In order for director Rick Rosenthal

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.300
to fully immerse us in
the world of Halloween,

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.960
there are many specific callbacks

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.440
to specific moments within
the first Halloween movie,

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.510
like how Karen suggests

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.540
her friend gets a ride home
from a Halloween party,

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.420
from a guy named Eddie Lee,
to which she responds...

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.410
- He's in Russellville.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.250
- [Jimmy] You might also remember

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.640
that the Haddonfield graves keeper

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.070
mentions a town called Russellville

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.050
in the first movie.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.850
- I remember over in Russellville,

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.440
old Charlie Bowles, about 15 years ago.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.640
- [Jimmy] When looking
at the news coverage

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.460
of the murders on Orange Grove Avenue,

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:19.360
one of the EMT's bud
makes this comparison.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.160
- It looks like a goddamn homecoming.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.730
- It's a really
interesting choice of words

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.120
because one of the main plot points

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.100
in the original Halloween regarded Laurie

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.360
and who she would choose to go
to the homecoming dance with.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.484
- [Annie] Well, you could ask Dick Baxter.

00:09:30.484 --> 00:09:32.907
He'd go out with you. (Annie laughs)

00:09:32.907 --> 00:09:34.030
- I'd rather go out with Ben Tramer.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.350
- [Zac] Ben Tramer also makes
an appearance in Halloween II,

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.500
or at least it's heavily
implied that the masked kid

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.390
who gets slammed by a
police car was Tramer.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.180
- Yeah, I'm worried about Bennett Tramer.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.417
- He isn't home yet.

00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:44.390
- [Boy In Blue Coat] Yeah
and he left the party at 10.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.373
- You're just gonna brush past the fact

00:09:45.373 --> 00:09:47.060
that the cop who just hit Ben Tramer

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.360
going 50 miles per hour,

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.730
gets out of his car and says,
"I didn't even see him."

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:51.790
Like you can't even give him

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.520
the benefit of the doubt on that one.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.530
- That part is pretty funny
if you're looking out for it.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.650
And I just love how the cop
basically goes out of his way

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:58.483
to hit the kid.

00:09:58.483 --> 00:09:59.827
His body is totally burned up,

00:09:59.827 --> 00:10:01.920
but the forensic dentist
also seems to think

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.620
that the victim is probably
around Tramer's age.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.580
On a night that feels

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.610
like it can't get any
worse for Laurie Strode,

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.660
Michael Myers is indirectly responsible

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:11.320
for the death of her biggest crush.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:12.910
Halloween has become the nightmare

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.270
that she can't wake up from.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.190
Then there's the security guy, Garrett.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.220
When we first meet him,
he's reading a newspaper.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.770
Let's zoom in on the headline here,

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.680
a dead ex-con with six
bullets in him will float.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.920
This probably refers
to the lung float test,

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.970
an autopsy procedure that
can help pathologists

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.610
determine the true cause of death.

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:31.430
But what I'm more interested
in here is six bullets.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.160
As you probably know if
you've seen the movie,

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.270
Dr. Loomis loaded Michael with six bullets

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:37.600
at the conclusion of
Halloween in the Doyle house.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.130
He proceeds to bring this
up whenever possible.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.440
- [Loomis] Tell the sheriff I shot him.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.010
I shot him six times.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.690
I shot him six times.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.518
And fired six shots into him-

00:10:46.518 --> 00:10:47.747
- You couldn't have shot him six times.

00:10:47.747 --> 00:10:49.110
- You think I'm lying, sheriff?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.020
- Speaking of Loomis,

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:51.970
there's also a scene
where he and the police

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.320
discover that Michael broke
into the elementary school.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.450
That's where they discover
the Samhain graffiti

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:57.420
that I mentioned earlier.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.540
When they enter the classroom,

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.130
they come across a childlike
drawing of a family of four

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.660
with a knife stuck into the sister.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.280
Obviously, we're led to believe
that this represents Judith,

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.420
the sister that Michael stabbed

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:07.750
in the opening of the first movie.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.680
But we later found out
in the infamous twist

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.470
that Laurie is Michael's other sister

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.660
and this drawing shows

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.440
that's the reason he's coming after her.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.300
If you look closely,

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.990
you'll see what appears
to be another figure

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.830
laying in the grass colored in red.

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:20.580
I'm guessing that's supposed to be Judith

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.420
and this is Laurie,

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.030
who Michael is threatening with the knife.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:26.040
The bigger question I
have is who drew this?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.440
Have Michael's art skills
not progressed since age six

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.440
due to his incarceration
in the sanitarium?

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.273
Are we supposed to believe

00:11:31.273 --> 00:11:32.800
that he made this drawing in kindergarten

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:33.880
and it's just been filed away

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.440
at the school somewhere ever since?

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.070
Or maybe it's just another kid's drawing

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:39.400
that he repurposed to
send his own message?

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.830
- Just don't even think about it.

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:43.370
Things will be better for you, I promise.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.120
- To be honest, I have a lot
of questions about this movie.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.560
Like, how did the media find out

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.610
about the babysitter murders

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.440
before the sheriff of the town?

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.500
Why does Loomis put his
face so close to Laurie

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.010
when he's asking if she's okay?

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:55.160
- I'm sorry I left you.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.000
Are you all right?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.030
- That's so weird.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.860
And why are there no
holes in Michael's mask

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.290
after Laurie shoots him in the face?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.200
Are we supposed to believe
that both of those shots

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.920
went perfectly into the eye holes?

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.770
Michael is 21 years old in this movie.

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:08.890
It's even called out by
Dr. Loomis at one point.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:11.860
So, why do the credits
say Michael Myers, age 23?

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.140
They actually made the same
mistake in the first movie.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.090
But if you do the math, he is 21.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.500
Not sure how that happens.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.220
Why does Michael's mask look
so funny from a low angle?

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:22.670
Was this entire thing just
an elaborate ruse by Jimmy

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.260
to get a lap dance from Laurie Strode?

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:27.370
- Men, you can't live with 'em,
you can't live without 'em.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.590
- Yeah, I don't think
that's how the saying goes.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:30.860
Help her out, Lloyd.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:34.970
- Women, can't live with
'em, can't live without 'em.

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.980
- Words of wisdom.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.830
The other question I've
always had about this movie

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.590
comes up in the third act
when Loomis, Marion Chambers,

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.410
and the state marshal
show up at the hospital,

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.770
not realizing that Laurie is
injured in the parking lot.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:46.720
I always found it pointless,

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.600
how she waits until
after they've gone inside

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:49.470
to scream for help,

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.660
but in analyzing this
movie, the scene fits in

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.740
with the bad dream theme
that's been established.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:55.160
Not being able to find your voice

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:56.810
totally sounds like
something that would happen

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:57.643
in a nightmare.

00:12:57.643 --> 00:12:59.540
I can even remember having
dreams like that as a kid,

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.650
and then waking up to find
myself mouthing the words

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:02.770
with a dry throat.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:03.603
I think the line

00:13:03.603 --> 00:13:05.530
that ties this movie's
themes together the best

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.030
comes when Loomis explains
the rituals of Samhain.

00:13:09.023 --> 00:13:10.777
(digital whooshing)

00:13:10.777 --> 00:13:11.870
- In order to appease the gods,

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:16.400
the Druid priests held fire rituals.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:20.940
Prisoners of war, criminals,
the insane, animals,

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:25.430
were burned alive in baskets.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.410
- It is interesting that
when he brings up rituals,

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.280
he specifically mentions burning alive

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.450
because, as we all know,

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.210
that's Michael Myers' fate in
this movie, at least for now.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.250
And that iconic shot of
Michael Myers burning

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:36.900
might be yet another direct reference

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.230
to The Thing from Another World,

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:40.840
which was referenced very
heavily in the first Halloween,

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.690
which was again,

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.710
a teaser for what John Carpenter
would go on to work on.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.150
- By observing the way they died,

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:48.953
the Druids believed they
could see omens of the future.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.713
2000 years later we've come no further.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:59.250
Samhain, isn't evil spirits.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:02.233
It isn't goblins, ghosts or witches.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.343
It's the unconscious mind.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:11.470
We're all afraid of the
dark inside ourselves.

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:14.060
- "We're all afraid of the
dark inside of ourselves."

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:15.360
The idea that I've come back to

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.740
throughout this entire video.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:19.100
The idea that Laurie
knows in her subconscious

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:20.770
that Michael Myers is her brother

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.490
is the terrifying reality
of this Halloween night.

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:26.650
A reality that makes even
evil spirits, goblins, ghosts,

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.860
and witches seem tame by comparison.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.850
The idea is hammered
home by the final scene,

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.300
bringing the story full circle.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.820
Laurie is right back where she started,

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:35.570
moving on to yet another hospital.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:36.600
The ambulance disappears

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.550
into what looks like a foggy dreamscape.

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.420
The news station, WWAR,

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.600
who we heard the initial reports
from about Michael Myers,

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.160
is now on the scene getting coverage

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.920
of his latest sets of victims.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.480
Michael lies face down on the ground,

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:49.150
seemingly defeated once more,

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.150
and the song that takes
us into the end credits

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:52.760
is none other than the song we heard

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:56.260
when this nightmare began,
Mr. Sandman, bring me a dream.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.830
This ending was meant to be
the death of Michael Myers,

00:14:58.830 --> 00:14:59.960
but as we now know,

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.750
the character was just too
profitable to stay dead.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.320
However, the next Halloween movie

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.340
focuses on a completely different story,

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.890
earning at the title of black sheep

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.360
of the Halloween franchise.

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.380
Another big thanks to Jimmy Champane

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.150
for breaking down this sequel with me.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.710
- Thanks again for having me on, Zac.

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.060
I usually talk about new news

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.610
related to the Halloween franchise,

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:20.450
so it's always nice to go back
and look at where it started.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.730
- I'd like to tell you to
go subscribe to his channel,

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.510
but legally I'm just not allowed to,

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:27.350
but I think just between you
and me, you know what to do.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.710
So, join us in the next
episode of Things You Missed,

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:30.970
as the season rolls over

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:34.060
and we discuss Halloween
III: Season of the Witch.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:37.310
Remember, subscribe to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week,

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.640
ring that death bell
for all notifications,

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:44.442
and I'll see you in the next
one, assuming we both survive.

00:15:44.442 --> 00:15:46.942
(eerie music)

